From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dash: Dock folders

Settings for the folders pinned to the dock, reading and writing the same
org.project_luma.shell-state keys the Shell does.

Show folders hides the rail without unpinning anything, so the folders keep
their places, their arrangements and their counts. Separate island takes
them out of the dock and gives them a surface of their own beside it, and
the preview draws that third surface. Both rows need a folder pinned before
they mean anything, and say so when there is none.

Each pinned folder is a row: its name, the path underneath it written the
way Files writes it, the arrangement it opens in (Stack or Grid, kept per
folder), buttons to move it along the rail, and one to take it off. Add
folder… opens a folder chooser. Taking a folder off the dock forgets its
arrangement, the stamp its count was measured against, and any position it
was last left in away from the dock, so nothing accumulates for folders that
are no longer there.

Every row is built only if the installed shell state has its key, so an
older one shows fewer rows rather than dead ones.

Generated against the g-c-c tree with 0001-0023 applied, for release
1.luma.27.preview20260920.1.
